    <DataNode elementId="AT1G02050-MONOMER" textLabel="AT1G02050-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O23674" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">LAP5 (AT4G34850) and LAP6 (AT1G02050) belong to the type III polyketide synthase (PKS) superfamily. In vitro assay of the LAP5 and LAP6 recombinant proteins detected multiple enzyme activities, which however does not include naringenin chalcone synthase activity. The recombinant protein was shown to condense one molecule of 4-coumaroyl-CoA with 2 molecule of malonyl-CoA to form trans- and cis-bisnoryangonin. However bisnoryangonin has been reported as an enzymatic &apos;derailment&apos; product (i.e., an incomplete biosynthetic product that detaches from the enzyme prior to completion of all the enzymatic steps). In addition, no presence of bisnoryangonin or its glycosides was detected in the Arabidopsis plants, indicating that bisnoryangonin is unlikely the in vivo physiological product of LAP5 and LAP6. The recombinant protein was also shown to catalyze condensation reactions using medium- and long-chain fatty acyl-CoA and malonyl-CoA as starter molecules, resulting in the formation of triketide (major products) and tetraketide (minor products) alpha-pyrone lipids. Again, pyrone lipids were not detected in Arabidopsis developing anthers, where LAP5 and LAP6 are supposed to express and function. As such, the physiological substrates and the biological functions of LAP5 and LAP6 remain unclear.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G02050-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G02050.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="O23674" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33586, RXN-18800, RXN-12837, RXN-12836" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G02050.1" />
